  "description": "The current linting setup runs in debug mode with a half\u2011second delay between checks, using a dark gutter theme. Highlights stay visible for 300\u202fseconds of inactivity, are demoted to the \u201ccomment\u201d scope when warnings appear while editing, and start hidden; old processes are retained. Linting operates in the background, and column highlights are enabled. The Python interpreter is set to **/usr/bin/python3**, while hover reports are shown for lines (but not regions). Marks appear in the minimap, and the panel will open on save in the current view. Syntax mapping translates\u202f*source.python*\u202fto\u202f*python*\u202fand\u202f*source.js*\u202fto\u202f*javascript*. The status bar displays counters as \u201c{error}/{warning}\u201d and messages as \u201c{message}\u201d, and it shows which linters are active.\n\nTwo linters are configured. **flake8** runs with the argument\u202f`--max-line-length=88`, is enabled, and inherits the environment variable\u202fPYTHONPATH\u202fset to\u202f`/my/project`. It is invoked directly as\u202f`flake8`, excludes files matching\u202f`tests/*`, works in background on files matching\u202f*source.python*, and uses\u202f`/my/project`\u202fas its working directory. Its style highlights errors and warnings with a squiggly underline (priority\u202f5) in the\u202fregion.yellowish\u202fscope, marked by the \ud83d\udc0d icon, and it specifically flags codes\u202fE501\u202fand\u202fW291. **eslint** runs with the argument\u202f`--config .eslintrc.json`, is also enabled, and is launched via\u202f`node ./node_modules/.bin/eslint`. It has no exclusions, runs on save for\u202f*source.js*\u202ffiles in\u202f`/my/js/project`, and highlights warnings with an outline (priority\u202f3) in the\u202fregion.orangish\u202fscope, marked by the \ud83c\udfe0 icon. Global style rules add a high\u2011priority (10) squiggly underline for errors in\u202fregion.redish\u202fwith a \ud83d\udea9 icon, and a low\u2011priority (2) fill for warnings in\u202fmarkup.warning\u202fwith a \u26a0\ufe0f icon. Experimental flags indicate the new UI is enabled while the beta feature is disabled."
